environ
	 Batch sizes, in processor order. Measured on the node (8x A100) on 2026-11-17
	DOWNLOAD_BATCH_SIZE 64	 Images per run of download_image. Network bound: 1.5 MB per PNG
	SPLIT_BATCH_SIZE 64	     Images per run of split_alpha. CPU only: it reads 1 PNG and writes 2
	ENCODE_BATCH_SIZE 128	 Images per run of encode_latents (about 40 s on one A100). run_proc_curate.fish starts two loops per GPU
	COLORBG_BATCH_SIZE 512	 Images per run of encode_colorbg. Big: a run costs ~40 s besides the encoding. run_proc_colorbg.fish starts 1 loop per GPU
	TRIMASK_BATCH_SIZE 512	        Images per run of each trimask_<method>. CPU only: it reads 1 PNG and writes 1 per variant. run_proc_trimask.fish starts 2 loops per method

	 Data
	MAGICK_REPO OneOverZero/MAGICK	 Hugging Face dataset: 140,955 RGBA PNGs, 1024 x 1024, straight alpha, 191 GB
	GRAY_LEVEL 0.5	                 Background of rgb_on_gray as a fraction of white: rgb * alpha + GRAY_LEVEL * (1 - alpha)
	EVAL_MODULUS 4000	             An image is eval, never trained on, when sha256(page_id) mod EVAL_MODULUS is 0: about 35 images

	 Models
	TEACHER_MODEL Efficient-Large-Model/SANA_Sprint_1.6B_1024px_teacher_diffusers	 The model we fine-tune. Its vae subfolder (DC-AE f32c32) makes the latents, so they match the model
	TEACHER_DIR ../models/Sana_Sprint_1.6B_1024px_teacher_diffusers	                 TEACHER_MODEL on FSx. encode_latents copies it to /models/sana-sprint-alpha-incontext once per machine

	 Eval (plan_eval, generate_eval)
	EVAL_SET resources/eval	 Eval images, captions and fixed noise, relative to the repo root. src/sana_alpha/eval_set.py makes it. Default of eval_models.eval_set
	EVAL_BATCH_SIZE 32	      eval_generations rows per run of generate_eval. A run costs ~12 s besides the GPU (8 rows took 15 s); a failed commit loses the run (FIBO2: 32 x 64 s = 34 min)
	EVAL_ONLY %	              SQL LIKE pattern of the eval_models tags generate_eval takes; env EVAL_ONLY overrides it, e.g. to run 4-step rows before a 30-step backlog

	 Trimask augmentations (trimask_<method>, manifest §13)
	TRIMASK_SUBSET 01	 A method uses a train image when the first hex digit of sha256(page_id + method) is one of these: about 17.6k images (m00653: ~16k)
	TRIMASK_COMPARE_MAX 005	 Every method also uses the train images whose sha256(page_id) starts at most with these 3 hex digits: about 200 images, the full rows of view_trimasks
	TRIMASK_VARIANTS 1	 Trimasks per image and method

	 Database
	DATABASE_PORT 23947	 Far from the ports of the Bluejay demos on the laptop (19471, 19683, 19783)

	 H3 Magic project (manifest §22): MiniMax H3 at 512 x 512, Pexels clips and MAGICK images
	H3_MAGICK_COUNT 10020	        MAGICK train images in h3_magick_images: the first by sha256(page_id); the first H3_VAL_COUNT of them are val
	H3_VAL_COUNT 20	                Held-out val rows per source, for validation loss. Never trained on
	H3_PEXELS_SELECTION h3magic/data/pexels_selection.parquet	 The Pexels clips (fork PexelsPick), relative to the repo root
	H3_IMAGE_BATCH_SIZE 256	        Images per run of h3_magick_image. CPU only
	H3_CUT_BATCH_SIZE 16	        Clips per run of h3_cut_clip. CPU: one 4K clip takes ~10 s to decode and crop
	H3_CAPTION_BATCH_SIZE 64	    Samples per run of h3_caption_*: all in flight at once, one Gemini call each (~30-60 s)
	H3_MIN_MOTION 1.5	            Least motion_512 (mean |frame - frame 0.5 s later|, 8-bit levels) of a clip to caption and train on
	H3_PEXELS_TRAIN 10000	        Pexels clips to train on: h3_choose_clip picks them by motion_512 and birdseye_score
	H3_PROVISIONAL_SHARE 0.40	    Train share of the cut clips while cutting (the final share is 10,000 / 21,503 = 0.46): a margin for clips that drop out
	H3_CHOOSE_FINAL false	        h3_choose_loop.fish sets env H3_CHOOSE_FINAL=true for the last run, after every clip is cut: exactly H3_PEXELS_TRAIN train

	 Latent Compositor (manifest §24): run_proc_latentcomp.fish imports its dataset and its scored candidates
	LC_DIR agents/.scratchpad/latentcomp	 Its folder, relative to the repo root: data/ (shards, test_plan.json) and r<k>/<name>/ (one folder per candidate)

	 DiffDec (manifest §26): run_proc_diffdec.fish imports its test set and its scored candidates
	DD_DIR agents/.scratchpad/diffdec	 Its folder, relative to the repo root: data/test/ (samples.json, one folder per sample), CONTRACT.md and g<round>/<name>/ (one folder per candidate)

database
	backend bluejay.local_database.LocalLanceBackend
	host 0.0.0.0
	port $DATABASE_PORT
	root lance
	fastlance	 Copied from MulticamDailies. Each setting is optional. Each comment tells what it does and its default
		commit_retry_time 365d	     When two processes save to one table at the same time, one must try again. This is how long it tries. Default 30s, then the save fails
		io_threads 256	             How many file reads one query does at the same time. Default 8 on local disk. 256 was 5-11% faster than 64 in MulticamDailies
		mem_pool 32GB	             Memory for large jobs, such as compaction. Default 150MB, which is too small for our large tables
		max_stale_time 0	         Fast mode: a query does not first look for new saves, so for this long it can miss rows that other processes saved. Default 0 (off)
		all_blobs_are_files true	 Each Blob value (a PNG or latent) is stored as its own file. Default true
		ram_cache 300GB	             Keeps the columns that queries read in RAM, so the next queries are faster. Never Blobs. Default off
		claim_pipeline write_behind	 Gives Claims faster, from rows that it found earlier and keeps in RAM; saves them after it answers. Default off

claims_table bluejay_claims
runs_table bluejay_runs
lineage_table bluejay_lineage
lineage true


 RULES FOR MAINTAINING THIS DTAB (copied from MulticamDailies' project.dtab, the house style):
 SEMANTIC BINDING: dtab-rules
    - One tab renders as four spaces. After each edit run: python3 agents/dtab_format.py check data/project.dtab (fix repairs the columns)
    - Formatting is part of the interface. Copy the alignment of nearby blocks exactly. Do not reformat what the user aligned by hand
    - These rules are for the AI. Keep the user's own prose in the user's voice: do not rewrite it
    - Everything is written in ASD-STE100
    - Sort tables and processors by dependency: an item comes after each item that it reads
    - Put the primary key first, then group the columns by the processor that writes them
    - Give each committed column a TYPE, a DESCRIPTION and an EXAMPLE
    - [Key] identifies a primary key. A tilde immediately before the type identifies a materialized field copied unchanged to the commit output,
      with no other use by the processor, including diagnostic logging.
    - Annotate each corresponding materialize and commit row that exists in the DTAB. Replace the space before the type with ~, as in [Key] ~str,
      without moving the columns. Preserve at least one space after the comment tab; widen the table if necessary. The marker is part of the comment, not the field name.
    - Write each processor's query inline in the processor. The queries section holds only queries for Sparrow
    - Delete a query that no processor or widget uses
    - Delete a processor file that this dtab does not use, in its own commit
    - Remove a note when it is resolved
    - Right-align values at their shared suffix, like numbers at the decimal point: ` 720p.mp4` under `1080p.mp4`
    - Lay out a big query's SELECT like view_dataset: one item per line, struct fields aligned
    - Write each query that is not tiny and simple as an annotated SQL query, like encode_latents' query, for a reader who does not speak SQL.
      An annotated SQL query has these properties in its FROM, JOIN and WHERE:
        - Break lines where the English breaks: each line is one short statement. Join lines that make one statement, like SELECT ... FROM
        - End each line with a tiny -- comment, so that the comments read down as one sentence
        - Align the comments one space after the longest line. Inside parentheses, indent the comment text 4 more, so the reader can skip it
        - Align the parts that nearby lines share, such as AND, IS, ON and =
    - Eval inference runs here as generate_eval (user, m00606, m00611). Judging the results is done by the agent (m00371)


tables

	bluejay_claims
		 Bluejay requires this table
		primary_key claim_id
		index	claim_id btree
		columns
			claim_id, run_id, claim_status string

	bluejay_runs
		 Bluejay requires this table
		primary_key run_id
		columns
			run_id, run_status, started_at, finished_at, processor, metadata, dtab, query string
			exit_code int64
			log blob
			profiler blob

	bluejay_lineage
		 Bluejay requires this table, because lineage is true
		columns
			claim_id, table string
			key, materialized map_(string(), binary())
			committed list_(string())

	import_jobs
		 One seeded row makes import_index read magick_index.tsv exactly once
		primary_key job_id
		columns
			job_id string
			index_tsv blob
		initial_rows
			,	job_id magick

	magick_samples
		 One row per MAGICK image: 140,955 rows when the download is done
		primary_key page_id
		columns
			page_id string

			 Written by import_index, from magick_index.tsv
			subject, color, split, source_claim_id, source_run_id string
			sim_score float64
			nsfw, hand_picked bool

			 Written by download_image
			rgba blob

			 Written by split_alpha
			alpha, rgb_on_gray blob
			alpha_coverage, alpha_soft_fraction, green_spill float64

			 Written by encode_latents
			latent_alpha_1024, latent_rgb_1024 blob
			vae_psnr_1024 float64

			 Written by encode_colorbg, for adapter_v2
			bg_color list_(float32(), 3)
			latent_rgb_colorbg_1024 blob

			 Written by encode_multires: long-lived per-GPU workers (data/processors/encode_multires.py, started by run_proc_trimask.fish), committed with Bluejay's commit, not Bluejay runs
			 latent_<x>_<S>: (32, S/32, S/32) bfloat16, key "latent", unscaled, of the image area-downsampled to S x S
			latent_rgb_768, latent_rgb_512, latent_rgb_256, latent_alpha_768, latent_alpha_512, latent_alpha_256 blob

			 Written by encode_fibo2 (manifest §14): long-lived per-GPU workers (data/processors/encode_fibo2.py, started by run_encode_fibo2.fish)
			 fibo2_<x>_<S>: (32, S/8, S/8) bfloat16, key "latent", the raw FLUX.2 VAE mode (not BatchNorm-normalized). gray = rgb_on_gray, colorbg = on bg_color
			fibo2_gray_1024, fibo2_gray_768, fibo2_gray_512, fibo2_gray_256, fibo2_colorbg_1024, fibo2_colorbg_768, fibo2_colorbg_512, fibo2_colorbg_256 blob

			 Written by encode_fibo2's job split (manifest §17, the splitter LoRA's targets; run_encode_fibo2.fish split): the same raw FLUX.2 VAE mode, of rgba on white and on black
			fibo2_white_1024, fibo2_white_768, fibo2_white_512, fibo2_white_256, fibo2_black_1024, fibo2_black_768, fibo2_black_512, fibo2_black_256 blob

			 Written by encode_fibo2's job matte (manifest §21, the matte adapter's target; run_encode_fibo2.fish matte): the same raw FLUX.2 VAE mode, of rgba's alpha as a gray image (3 equal channels)
			fibo2_matte_1024, fibo2_matte_768, fibo2_matte_512, fibo2_matte_256 blob

	eval_models
		 One row per model to evaluate. To evaluate a new checkpoint, add a row here: run_proc_eval.fish initializes first
		primary_key model_tag
		columns
			model_tag, pipeline, checkpoint, prompt_variant, eval_set string	 Empty eval_set = EVAL_SET
			steps int64
			guidance float64
		initial_rows
			,	model_tag sprint_plain										pipeline sprint		checkpoint stock														prompt_variant plain		steps 2		guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag sprint_gray										pipeline sprint		checkpoint stock														prompt_variant gray			steps 2		guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag teacher_plain										pipeline teacher	checkpoint stock														prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag teacher_gray										pipeline teacher	checkpoint stock														prompt_variant gray			steps 20	guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag adapter_toy_ddp2_step000400						pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/adapter/toy_ddp2/step_000400							prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag control_overfit_test_step000400					pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400						prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag final_overfit_test_step000400						pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/final_step_000400				prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			 Step 5 transfer: a control step on the sprint pipeline = stock student + merged control LoRA + gates
			,	model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_1step			pipeline sprint		checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400						prompt_variant plain		steps 1		guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_2step			pipeline sprint		checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400						prompt_variant plain		steps 2		guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag transfer_overfit_test_step000400_4step			pipeline sprint		checkpoint models/control/overfit_test/step_000400						prompt_variant plain		steps 4		guidance 4.5
			 Step 2: the real adapter run
			,	model_tag adapter_v1_step001000								pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/adapter/adapter_v1/step_001000						prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			 The adapter that control_v1 is trained on
			,	model_tag adapter_v1_step002000								pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/adapter/adapter_v1/step_002000						prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			 Step 3, 4 and 5 of control_v1 step 500: control on the adapter, final (no adapter), and transfer onto Sprint
			,	model_tag control_v1_step000500								pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/control/control_v1/step_000500						prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
			,	model_tag final_v1_step000500								pipeline teacher	checkpoint models/control/control_v1/final_step_000500					prompt_variant plain		steps 20	guidance 4.5
